Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Sample Kinetic Fitting", "Title",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.950264485196907*^9, 
  3.9502644918604794`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"83570342-42bb-ca40-8d49-\
53c24ddb2422"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Importing data into variables", "Section",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.9502669465905*^9, 
  3.9502669584844418`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"cf896d35-6cd9-b148-9381-\
9acfdbaf9f94"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The first step in enzyme kinetic data fitting is to import the data, \
requiring the correct file path. The text ",
 StyleBox["data =",
  FontFamily->"Courier New",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 0.]],
 " tells Mathematica to store your imported data in a variable called \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]data.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \n\nIf you are using the \
app, you can type ",
 StyleBox["Import[\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]",
  FontFamily->"Courier New",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 0.]],
 " and after you add that last \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote] \
you\[CloseCurlyQuote]ll see a button called \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]File \
Browser.\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] Click on that to locate your data file. \n\n\
Otherwise, you can have Mathematica add the file path by going through the \
Insert tab, followed by \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]File Path...\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]\n\nPut ",
 StyleBox["//TableForm",
  FontFamily->"Courier New",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 0.]],
 " at the end of the line to get the data to display in columns.  Hit ",
 StyleBox["\[ShiftKey]",
  FontSize->24,
  FontWeight->"Normal",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0., 0., 0.]],
 " + ",
 StyleBox["\[EnterKey]",
  FontSize->24],
 " to execute the command.\n"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.950264594828514*^9, {3.9502648659615593`*^9, 3.950264980737385*^9}, {
   3.9502651996505623`*^9, 3.950265213302824*^9}, {3.9502652816854763`*^9, 
   3.9502653562156734`*^9}, {3.9582113986155453`*^9, 
   3.958211487274979*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"80f5a377-ac60-4d49-a6fe-\
d1f32719d0ad"],

